local _, ns = ...

ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "7.0.11", text = "Surnames on their own, spell ranks in a drawer, smarter party spells on the radials, and threat numbers that agree with each other.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffThreat numbers|r as a tank in a dungeon: nameplates, target frame and meter.\n• |cffffffffNameplates|r in big pulls: their auras, and how smooth it feels.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r the new rank drawer, and party spells while you're alone.\n• |cffffffffLoot Roll Window:|r |cffffffffFade in Combat|r, with a real roll during a fight.\n• |cffffffffNameplates|r with |cffffffffSmooth Animated Bars|r: its colours on our plates.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting:|r |cffffffffWarn Before Selling Set Gear|r and |cffffffffWarn Before Selling Quest Items|r are gone for now. They may have caused items to be blocked by the game.\n• |cffffffffMeters:|r with |cffffffffTank's Lead|r on, the tank's percent is now their threat against second place, like \"125%\". It used to show \"100% (+25%)\".\n• |cffffffffParty and Raid Frames:|r |cffffffffShow Name|r is now a list on raid frames and the party's Raid Style: Off, First Name, Last Name or Full Name. Your choice is kept.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffShow Full Name|r for Name Only plates is now |cffffffffShow Name|r: First Name, Last Name or Full Name. Your choice is kept.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r a party spell you use alone goes to your friendly target first.\n• |cffffffffNameplates|r with |cffffffffSmooth Animated Bars|r: a theme picked for nameplates there now colours our plates.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffLast Name|r on unit frames and nameplates.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r one entry per spell, with every rank in a drawer.\n• |cffffffffThreat numbers|r are the same on nameplates, unit frames and the meter.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Names|r\n• |cffffffffLast Name|r in every name list:\n      - Health Text and Name Above Frames on unit frames\n      - Show Name on raid frames and the party's Raid Style\n      - Health Text, Names Above Plate and Name Only on nameplates\n• Someone without a surname shows their name.\n• Forever Style keeps its own name.\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• |cffffffffSpell ranks:|r the Catalog shows each spell once. Adding it gives you your best rank.\n      - The small arrow on its icon opens every rank.\n      - Search still finds single ranks, like \"rank 3\".\n      - With a controller, the Catalog still lists every rank.\n• |cffffffffParty spells:|r alone, they go to your friendly target, and to you when you have none. The button shows your target's name.\n• |cffffffffUses left:|r spells that need a reagent show how many uses you have, like the action bars.\n\n|cffe6cc99Loot Rolls|r\n• |cffffffffFade in Combat|r (off) in Edit Mode, for the Loot Roll Window. These bring it back:\n      - Pointing at it\n      - The last 5 seconds of a roll you haven't decided on\n      - The end of the fight\n• |cffffffffFaded Opacity|r (30): how see-through it gets.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffSetup tour|r (|cffffd100/fui tour|r): new pages for Nameplates, for Bags & Looting, and for Buffs and Reminders. The Cooldown Manager is now part of the Bars page.\n• |cffffffffNameplates|r with |cffffffffSmooth Animated Bars|r:\n      - A theme picked under its Nameplates shows on our plates.\n      - With its |cffffffffYour Colours on Their Bars|r on, plates and your target's DoT marker work again, if plates and target both have a theme. Game Colour and Class Color keep FlareUI's fill.\n• |cffffffffPerformance:|r\n      - Less work each frame on nameplates, the dispel glow and the chat.\n      - New nameplates load their buffs and debuffs a few plates at a time, for smaller spikes in big pulls.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffThreat:|r as a tank in a dungeon, nameplates could stay at 100%, and unit frames could show no number.\n• |cffffffffThreat:|r nameplates, unit frames and the meter could show different numbers for the same mob.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r a lower rank of a party spell could turn into your best rank. It now stays, and its rank shows in the list." },
    { version = "7.0.10", text = "A hotfix for quest clicks that only opened the quest log, plus Smooth Animated Bars on nameplates.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r clicking quests from other zones, and Craftsman's Writs.\n• |cffffffffNameplates|r with |cffffffffSmooth Animated Bars|r: please tell us how it looks and runs.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r support for |cffffffffSmooth Animated Bars|r. Its own nameplate switches turn the liquid on.\n      - With its DoTs on Nameplates on, your DoTs show on your target's plate.\n      - With its |cffffffffYour Colours on Their Bars|r on, nameplates keep FlareUI's fill.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r clicking a quest from another zone, or one with no location like a Craftsman's Writ, often opened only the quest log.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r with the map open full size, or with its quest list closed, some quests didn't open." },
    { version = "7.0.9", text = "A bug-fixing update: we went through the open reports and fixed as many as we could. It also adds sharper outlines for every font.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing.|r These were hard to reproduce, so please tell us if they're fixed for you:\n• |cffffffffController:|r walking while a radial is open, and placing a radial on a controller button.\n• |cffffffffBlocked items:|r potions, armor kits and quest items that the game blocked. If it happens again, send us what |cffffd100/fui errors|r shows.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r switching tabs during a fight.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r clicking a quest while the map is open on a zone.\n• |cffffffffDruids:|r |cffffffffKeep Page 1 in Stealth|r.\n• |cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack:|r if its section stays empty, send us what |cffffd100/fui errors|r shows.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffAction Bars:|r gryphons with a changed |cffffffffScale|r may move once, to where Edit Mode has them saved.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r Questie's quest icon sits beside the plate, left of the level box. If you moved it in Questie to make up for our plates, set it again there.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r with |cffffffffColour Names by Class|r, names on class-coloured bars are a lighter shade.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r bars fill their border, so the whole plate is about 2 pixels smaller. The bar keeps its size.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r player and link icons are as big as the text.\n• |cffffffffChat and Meters:|r with |cffffffffBorder|r on None and |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r at 0%, the line under the header hides too.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting:|r Bank Window and Vendor have their own |cffffffffBank & Vendor|r tab.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffSharp Outline|r for every font.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r Name Only has its own font.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r whispers bring a faded chat back.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Fonts|r\n• |cffffffffSharp Outline|r in every |cffffffffOutline|r list: cleaner edges at any size. Some fonts draw stray lines with it.\n• |cffffffffOutline|r (Each Font's Own) on the General page, under Global Font: one outline for every FlareUI font. Needs a reload.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffName Only|r on the Fonts tab: its own font, size, outline and shadow. It starts as your Names font.\n      - |cffffffffName Only Size|r is now a % of that font.\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r is a list: Off, In a Group, In an Instance or Always. If you had it on, it's on Always.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffWarn Before Selling Set Gear|r (off): asks before you sell gear from a saved equipment set. By BillChirico.\n• |cffffffffWarn Before Selling Quest Items|r (off): asks before you sell quest items. By BillChirico.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bug reports|r\n• |cffffd100/fui errors|r says more about blocked items.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r near a screen edge, it moves in so every button fits. Nothing is picked until you move the mouse.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting:|r the Tools section is called |cffffffffTweaks|r.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r whispers, Battle.net ones too, bring a faded chat back even when another tab is shown.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r every popped-out window that takes a message comes back, not only the first.\n• |cffffffffMinimap:|r the Info Bar's gold uses the bags' coins, size and gaps.\n• |cffffffffBags:|r |cffffffffAuto Open Containers|r waits while an armor kit or a spell is waiting for its item.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r fewer updates for the same result. By parchinskiy.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffGamepad UI:|r\n      - Another try at walking while a radial is open.\n      - Placing a radial on a controller button could fail with \"Failed to pick up an action\".\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r clicking a quest with the map open on a zone didn't open the quest.\n• |cffffffffAction Bars:|r gryphons with a changed |cffffffffScale|r moved at every login.\n• |cffffffffAction Bars:|r another try at |cffffffffKeep Page 1 in Stealth|r showing the Prowl page (druids).\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r there was a dark gap between the bars and their border.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r Questie's quest icon sat over the level box on your target.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode:|r with Snap on, the minimap and the chat stopped short of the screen edge.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r\n      - Another try at tabs that don't switch during a fight: they could stay stuck with the |cffffffffMeter Tab|r on.\n      - With |cffffffffFade Delay|r at 0, new messages never brought the chat back.\n      - In a fade group, changing |cffffffffVisibility|r on another frame could turn off New Messages.\n      - With |cffffffffFade Old Lines|r, lines could start fading under the mouse.\n• |cffffffffBags:|r another try at the crafting bag missing from the combined backpack with |cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack|r on.\n• |cffffffffSync Blizz UI:|r other characters were asked to reload when nothing had really changed.\n• |cffffffffBuff Reminders:|r another try at potions and kits blocked by the game.\n• |cffffffffRaid Frames:|r click-casting didn't work on the main tanks' targets.\n• |cffffffffMeters:|r the warning about Blizzard's own Visibility setting could be missed.\n• |cffffffffSettings:|r |cffffffffShow Item Level|r showed a player in its preview." },
    { version = "7.0.8", text = "A small fix for errors in group content, with two more fixes from your reports.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffUnit Frames:|r |cffffffffValues on Mouseover|r spammed errors in dungeons and raids.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r with |cffffffffNames Above Plate|r, names could show the colour of another player or enemy.\n• |cffffffffMinimap:|r an error in the addon drawer with addons that put thousands of pins on the minimap." },
    { version = "7.0.7", text = "A big round of controller work, a real second power slot for druids in Forever Style, and a long list of fixes from your reports.\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffController players:|r we don't all play with one, so the controller changes below need your hands. Tell us what works and what doesn't.\n• |cffffffffDruids:|r try |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r in Forever Style, in and out of fights.\n• If the game says it blocked an action from FlareUI, send us what |cffffd100/fui errors|r shows. It now lists those too.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffQuality of Life:|r the |cffffffffNameplates|r tab is gone.\n      - |cffffffffCombo Points|r, |cffffffffQuest Objectives|r and the |cffffffffIn Combat|r choices are in the Nameplates module, and work with Quality of Life off. Your choices carry over.\n      - These are gone from Blizzard's own nameplates: Combo Points, Quest Objectives, Hide Names, Hide Level Box and Level Before Names.\n• |cffffffffForever Style:|r |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r no longer cuts the power bar in half. The mana bar has its own slot below the frame.\n• |cffffffffGamepad UI:|r these are off, because each could break the controller until a reload:\n      - stick scrolling in the quest tracker\n      - opening quests from a click in FlareUI's tracker, and linking them to chat\n      - the meter's right-click menus\n      - the FlareUI button in the ESC menu\n      - the chat's Copy button\n      - |cffffffffSkip Loot Confirmations|r\n• |cffffffffGamepad UI:|r synced chat settings and the chat style wait for a reload or logout.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r use all of it with a controller.\n• |cffffffffForever Style:|r Blizzard's own second power slot for druids.\n• |cffffffffParty Frames:|r raid markers on what your party is targeting.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Gamepad UI|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r LB + RB, then D-pad Up, gives the controller to FlareUI's tracker. A legend below it shows the buttons.\n      - D-pad: moves between quests, quest items, zones, recipes and the header buttons\n      - A: focuses a quest, uses an item, folds a zone\n      - X: opens the quest on the map\n      - Y: a list with Share Quest, Collapse, Pin to Top and Untrack\n      - B: gives the controller back\n      - In fights, only quest items work. With none on screen, or with no tracker on screen, the quest log opens instead.\n• |cffffffffDialogs:|r X picks the third answer.\n\n|cffe6cc99Party Frames|r\n• |cffffffffShow Target Markers|r (off) in Edit Mode under Pets & Targets: the raid marker of what each member is targeting, on the right edge of its frame. Needs |cffffffffParty Targets|r on.\n• |cffffffffRaid Style:|r |cffffffffHealth Text|r and |cffffffffPower Text|r have Left, Centre and Right, like Classic. Your old pick stays in the centre.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bug reports|r\n• |cffffd100/fui errors|r also lists what the game blocked from FlareUI.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffForever Style:|r with |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r, the power bar and its numbers keep their size, and it works with |cffffffffPower Height|r off. The attached cast bar and the auras below the frame make room.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu|r (controller):\n      - You keep walking when a radial opens.\n      - The lit button is always the one that's used.\n      - The camera stays still for a moment after it closes.\n      - A radial closes on loading screens.\n• |cffffffffMinimap:|r the Info Bar's text is white.\n• |cffffffffBuff Reminders:|r the missing elixir ranks are in the list. By GregDuhamel.\n• |cffffffffGerman:|r 42 phrases translated. By kluntjewalker.\n• |cffffffffHungarian:|r translated up to 7.0.6. By Xentinus.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffGamepad UI:|r\n      - The quest shortcut (D-pad Up) gave the controller to a tracker nobody could see.\n      - FlareUI's quest tracker took the stick while a radial was open.\n      - B could close a radial opened from a B slot right away.\n      - The dialogs and the settings window could pass button presses on to the game.\n      - Several ways FlareUI's chat could stop the controller from working until a reload.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r clicking a quest's text could open the map without the quest.\n• |cffffffffSettings:|r the X didn't close the window in a fight.\n• |cffffffffFonts:|r a name's shadow could be missing, most visibly with |cffffffffOutline|r on None.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r\n      - |cffffffffCombo Points|r didn't show with Quality of Life off.\n      - The level didn't show with |cffffffffNames Above Plate|r and |cffffffffLevel|r on Follow Name.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r\n      - Toys didn't work from a radial.\n      - Long names in the Catalog ran into its title.\n• |cffffffffBuff Reminders:|r a drink could still be remembered as your food.\n• |cffffffffMinimap:|r icon tooltips showed a second tooltip about moving them.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r another try at tabs that don't switch during a fight. |cffffffffIf yours still don't, please tell us.|r" },
}
